WEBVTT

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.470
Access control should cover facilities, aircraft, controllers, applications,

00:00:04.470 --> 00:00:09.000
drone accounts, planning tools, data stores, dashboards, networks, backups, and exports.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.340
Use individual accounts, least privilege, strong authentication,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:14.210
and timely removal of stale access.

00:00:14.210 --> 00:00:17.800
Protect firmware and software through approved update, configuration,

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.240
and vulnerability-management processes.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.660
Inventory versions and dependencies, review changes,

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:26.140
and ensure crews are not quietly operating different configurations.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:29.120
Network security includes segmentation, secure remote access,

00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:32.965
monitored administrative activity, protected wireless services, secrets management,

00:00:32.965 --> 00:00:35.000
and controlled integrations.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:39.190
Avoid exposing management interfaces or sensitive telemetry unnecessarily.

00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:40.921
Privacy review begins at mission intake.

00:00:40.921 --> 00:00:44.960
Define purpose, area, detail, people affected, notice or consent where required,

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:47.000
minimization, access, sharing, and retention.

00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:51.210
A legal flight can still create intrusive or disproportionate collection.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:56.000
Audit logs and regulatory documentation support accountability.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:59.350
Preserve approvals, qualifications, maintenance, flights, warnings, access, exports,

00:00:59.350 --> 00:00:59.890
incidents,

00:00:59.890 --> 00:01:03.185
and retention actions at a level appropriate to the operation and current requirements.

00:01:03.185 --> 00:01:07.100
Responsible-use policy prohibits harassment, stalking, unlawful surveillance,

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:12.230
weaponization, restriction bypass, unsafe operations, and targeting private individuals.

00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:14.000
Compliance is not paperwork around the mission;

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:17.000
it is the evidence that the program deserves trust.

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.000
Third-party platforms and service providers belong in the security review.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.000
Evaluate data location, administrative access, retention, subcontractors,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:27.965
incident notification, export capability, account recovery,

00:01:27.965 --> 00:01:30.000
and what happens when the contract ends.
